Keyword leg alone for the NVDA figure query (no embedding; ts_rank_cd over the latest EMBEDDED NVDA filing per type,
terms 'fiscal' | '2026' | 'revenue' | '215,938' | 'up' | '65'): positions 1..5 are chunks 806, 842, 881, 864, 873 (none contains
215,938); the chunk with the "Revenue $ 215,938 $ 130,497 Up 65%" row (802, ITEM_7) is sixth. Recorded in RAG.md as the
fusion-tuning observation (RAG-12).

Decision (plan rule: enable by default only if hit@5 improves and no ticker's hit@5 decreases):
  hit@5 0.600000 -> 0.633333 improves; AAPL 0.9 -> 0.9, MSFT 0.6 -> 0.7, NVDA 0.3 -> 0.3, none lower  => rag.retrieval.hybrid-enabled: true
  (application.yaml and FilingRetrievalProperties; FilingRetrievalServiceTests asserts the property default.)
  Floor: 0.633333 - 0.1 = 0.533333, rounded down to a multiple of 0.05 = 0.50, not below the current 0.50 => rag.evaluation.min-hit-at-5 stays 0.50.
  Question-level regressions the ticker rule does not see (msft-04 1 -> 8, msft-01 6 -> 10) are logged as Follow_Ups RAG-12.

Code in this milestone: the yaml/property default flip, and reciprocalRankScores now increments the per-list rank after the
duplicate check (unit assertion: [a, a, b] scores a = 1/61, b = 1/62). Tests that relied on the old default set hybrid off explicitly.

